.TH SETFONT 1.SH NAMEsetfont \- load a downloadable terminal font.SH SYNOPSIS\fBsetfont\fRpath.SH DESCRIPTION\fBsetfont\fRloads the character font in\fIpath\fRinto a terminal that accepts downloaded fonts, from Thomas Wolk's EFFOutilities.  With no argument it answers\fBusage: setfont <path>\fR.\fR.PPUnder os9exec, given a font file it writes nothing to the terminal, to\fB$PORT\fR,\fRor to a file\fBPORT\fRnames, and returns 0; the terminal it was written for is not here toreceive one..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR